    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something I find both challenging and rewarding. While my formal education lacked rigorous math training, my curiosity for patterns in nature (like birdwatching) or logic in coding keeps me engaged. It’s not about memorization but understanding how structures work, which aligns with my love for philosophy’s exploration of meaning.",
